1. Derived from Herdr (Apache License 2.0)
------------------------------------------

Herdr is developed by herdrdev (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-app) and is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, the same license as this repository. Herdr's own layouts and mods are shipped with the app, readable on
every installation, and the Herdr documentation tells people to clone them (`layout.clone`, `mod.clone`) and edit the
clones. Redistributing such clones is allowed under the Apache License 2.0 provided this notice and the statement of
changes below travel with them. Each clone records its source in its `cloned_from` field.

Modified copies (all taken from Herdr 0.1.12):

  layouts/portrait.json            from the layout `main`
  layouts/portrait-bottom.json     from the layout `main`
      Changes: new node tree (a full-width bar of space columns above or below the work area, a tab strip, a hidden
      right panel with Files and Changes); the sidebar and the Spaces and Agents lists removed; no theme pinned; root
      `preview` field added.
  mods/portrait-tabs/             from the mod `tabs`
      Changes: the Files and Changes buttons moved to mods/bar-strip; the per-space memory of the right panel kept
      here; icons copied into the mod; assets renamed to the new folder.
  mods/portrait-pane/             from the mod `pane`
      Changes: a mod's pane without a title is named after its mod; icons copied into the mod; assets renamed to the
      new folder.
  mods/portrait-files/            from the mod `files`
      Changes: a click on a file opens it in nvim in a floating window (mods/nvim-float) instead of a preview, with
      the read-only preview kept for Alt-click and for Windows; a title was added to mod.json.
  mods/portrait-changes/          from the mod `changes` of Herdr 0.1.13
      Changes: a list of the repo's worktrees and the folders you add, each opening in place, instead of only the
      focused pane's repo; the pure parts moved to logic.mjs; icons copied into the mod; a title was added to mod.json.

Not redistributed: Herdr's other mods (`workspace-status`, `picker`, `machine-add`, `menu`, `new-menu`)
are only used by name; they come with the person's Herdr and are never copied into this repository.


2. Icons copied from Herdr 0.1.12 (Apache License 2.0; glyphs: Lucide, ISC, and MIT)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These small SVG pictures are byte-for-byte or whitespace-only copies of files in Herdr 0.1.12's shipped mods, placed in
the mod folder that draws them (a mod may not load another mod's files: Herdr replaces its shipped mods on every update).
The folder after the arrow is where the file comes from in Herdr.

What Herdr says about them. Herdr's repository (`defaults/icons/LICENSES.md`) states: "Glyphs ... including icons in
shipped mods: Lucide, ISC, with MIT-licensed Feather-derived icons". Some of the files differ from Lucide's current
drawing (other stroke width or radius); those are Herdr's own work, and Herdr's license is Apache-2.0. This repository
cannot tell the two apart file by file, so it keeps both notices: the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE), and the ISC and MIT
texts reproduced in section 3.

  spinner.svg                      mods/portrait-tree, mods/portrait-tabs, mods/portrait-pane   -> workspace-chrome
